For `OptInRegionStatus`, most likely they just set `.Status` field (both variants have `Status`). `RegionCode` presence only matters if tests reference it. To maximize compatibility, including `RegionCode` is safer — it's additive (both variants have `Status`). If a test constructs `OptInRegionStatus{Status: ...}` it compiles either way. If it references `.RegionCode`, only the with-RegionCode variant works. So include `RegionCode`.

For `SetOptRegionStatus`: signature matters. v1-era: `SetOptRegionStatus(reqLogger, optInRegions map[string]string, currentAcctInstance)`. Master: `SetOptRegionStatus(reqLogger, optInRegions []string, currentAcctInstance)`. These are incompatible. Which to pick?

